      "name": "FormatNumberWithSeparators",
      "signature": "void FormatNumberWithSeparators(uint dwValue, Unicode * pwszOutput, int nMaxLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Formats an unsigned integer as a Unicode string with thousands separators.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nMaxLength >= 3 or assert\n2. Convert dwValue to decimal string via itoa (base 10)\n3. Calculate output length: strlen + (strlen-1)/3 commas\n4. Copy digits right-to-left, inserting comma (0x2C) every 3 digits\n5. If number is 0 or buffer too small, output \"0\"\n\nParameters:\n- dwValue (uint): Number to format\n- pwszOutput (Unicode*): Output buffer for formatted string\n- nMaxLength (int): Maximum characters including null terminator\n\nReturns:\n- void (output via pwszOutput parameter)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2C (44): ASCII/Unicode comma separator\n- 3: Digits between separators (thousands grouping)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:a3213e30922ffab27fd88db94ad2c955",
