      "name": "IntToStringRadix",
      "signature": "void IntToStringRadix(uint dwValue, char * szBuffer, uint dwRadix, int nNegative)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts an unsigned integer to a string with specified radix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nNegative is set, prepend '-' and negate value\n2. Extract digits via repeated division by radix\n3. Convert digit: 0-9 become '0'-'9', 10-35 become 'a'-'z'\n4. Null-terminate the string\n5. Reverse digit portion to get correct order\n\nParameters:\n- dwValue (uint): Unsigned value to convert\n- szBuffer (char*): Output buffer for string result\n- dwRadix (uint): Number base (10 for decimal, 16 for hex)\n- nNegative (int): Non-zero to prepend '-' and negate\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in szBuffer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c147e94384608ec25ec11bdc009b5d4a",
