      "name": "Int64ToCharInternal",
      "signature": "void Int64ToCharInternal(uint dwValueLo, uint dwValueHi, char * szOutput, uint dwRadix, int nIsSigned)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Converts a 64-bit integer to a string representation in the specified radix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nIsSigned != 0, prepend '-' and negate the 64-bit value\n2. Combine dwValueLo/dwValueHi into 64-bit longlong\n3. Loop: divide by radix, convert remainder to digit ('0'-'9' or 'a'-'z')\n4. Null-terminate and reverse the digit string in-place\n\nParameters:\n- dwValueLo (uint): Low 32 bits of the 64-bit value\n- dwValueHi (uint): High 32 bits of the 64-bit value\n- szOutput (char*): Output buffer for the string\n- dwRadix (uint): Numeric base (e.g., 10 for decimal, 16 for hex)\n- nIsSigned (int): If non-zero, treat value as signed and add '-' prefix\n\nReturns:\n- void (result written to szOutput buffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x30 ('0'): ASCII offset for digits 0-9\n- 0x57 ('W'): ASCII offset for lowercase hex digits a-z (0x57 + 10 = 0x61 = 'a')",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f50cef55e3995b71878cb37679f6c2d6",
