      "name": "ParseTokenWithDelimiters",
      "signature": "byte * ParseTokenWithDelimiters(byte * pbStr, byte * pbDelims)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Tokenizes a string using a set of delimiter characters (strtok-like).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get TLS thread data for static state\n2. Build 256-bit bitmap from delimiter string (1 bit per ASCII value)\n3. If pbStr is NULL, resume from saved position in TLS[6]\n4. Skip leading delimiters in input string\n5. Scan for next delimiter or end-of-string\n6. If found delimiter, null-terminate token and save position to TLS[6]\n7. Return token start or NULL if no token found\n\nParameters:\n- pbStr (byte*): Input string or NULL to continue tokenizing\n- pbDelims (byte*): Null-terminated string of delimiter characters\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to extracted token, or NULL if no more tokens\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): TLS offset for saved position (TLS[6])\n- 32: Size of delimiter bitmap (256 bits / 8)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:89f4dd5ffbabb9ad6d64be0e709db24d",
