      "name": "GetCharTypeFlags",
      "signature": "uint GetCharTypeFlags(void * this, int nCharCode, uint dwTypeMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Gets character type flags for a Unicode code point with locale awareness.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If character code < 0x100, use direct table lookup in g_pwCharTypeTable\n2. Otherwise, check if high byte indicates lead byte (0x80 flag in table)\n3. If lead byte: construct 2-byte MBCS sequence (swapped byte order)\n4. If not lead byte: construct 1-byte sequence with char only\n5. Call FUN_6fc47053 (GetStringTypeW/A wrapper) to get type flags\n6. Return flags masked with dwTypeMask\n\nParameters:\n- nCharCode (int): Unicode code point to check\n- dwTypeMask (uint): Bitmask for type flags to return (C1_DIGIT=0x4, C1_SPACE=0x8, etc.)\n- IMPLICIT: ECX is garbage (not a true this pointer)\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero if char has specified type flags, 0 otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100 (256): ASCII range boundary\n- 0x80: Lead byte indicator flag in character type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d858691b25ff9d68f1965dc04bb2a9aa",
