      "name": "WriteCharToBuffer",
      "signature": "void WriteCharToBuffer(uint dwChar, FILE * pFile, int * pnBytesWritten)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a single character to a FILE buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement buffer count (pFile->_cnt)\n2. If space available, write char directly to buffer\n3. If buffer full, call FlushBufferWriteChar to flush and write\n4. Update bytes written counter (increment on success, set -1 on error)\n\nParameters:\n- dwChar (uint): Character to write (low byte used)\n- pFile (FILE*): File stream with buffer\n- pnBytesWritten (int*): Counter incremented on success\n\nReturns:\n- void (error signaled via pnBytesWritten = -1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xffffffff (-1): Error indicator from FlushBufferWriteChar\n\nNotes:\n- piVar1, uVar2 are decompiler phantom variables (cannot be renamed)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:48de6fa61a4bf40c36c288aa452eb3ad",
