      "name": "WriteRepeatedCharToBuffer",
      "signature": "void WriteRepeatedCharToBuffer(uint dwCharCode, int nRepeatCount, int * pnFormatCtrl, int * pnWrittenCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a character repeatedly to a format buffer.\n\nUsed by ProcessFormatString to output padding characters\n(spaces for right-alignment, zeros for numeric padding).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nRepeatCount > 0, exit if not\n2. Enter loop, decrement count each iteration\n3. Call WriteCharToBuffer with character code\n4. Check pnWrittenCount for error (-1)\n5. Exit early on error, else continue until count exhausted\n\nParameters:\n- dwCharCode (uint): ASCII character code (0x20=space, 0x30=zero)\n- nRepeatCount (int): Number of times to write the character\n- pnFormatCtrl (int*): Format control/FILE stream pointer\n- pnWrittenCount (int*): Running byte count, set to -1 on error\n\nReturns:\n- void (error state communicated via pnWrittenCount)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f7657de81ac8d5d29214c35b4fa6fd17",
