      "name": "GetHeapBlockSize",
      "signature": "SIZE_T GetHeapBlockSize(void * pBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Gets the usable size of a heap-allocated memory block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check heap mode (g_dwHeapMode)\n2. If mode 3: Lock critical section, get block info via FUN_6fc481cf,\n   calculate size as (block[-4] - 9), unlock\n3. If mode 2: Lock critical section, get small block info via FUN_6fc48f2a,\n   calculate size as (first_byte << 4), unlock\n4. If block lookup fails or other mode: call HeapSize directly\n\nParameters:\n- pBlock (void*): Pointer to allocated memory block\n\nReturns:\n- SIZE_T: Usable size of the block in bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:eef5ae1e69543f2ca247fd0a568bf7f0",
