      "name": "HeapAllocBase",
      "signature": "void * HeapAllocBase(size_t cbSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Base heap allocation with multi-tier strategy.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If heap mode is 3 (SBH), try small block heap if size <= threshold\n2. If heap mode is 2 (page heap), align size to 16 bytes, try page alloc if <= threshold\n3. Fall back to HeapAlloc with 16-byte aligned size\n\nParameters:\n- cbSize (size_t): Requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated memory, or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10 (16): Minimum allocation size and alignment\n- 0xf: Mask for 16-byte alignment calculation\n- 0x3: Heap mode for Small Block Heap (SBH)\n- 0x2: Heap mode for Page Heap\n- 0x9: CRT critical section ID for heap",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
