      "name": "FreeIoInfoTableEntries",
      "signature": "void FreeIoInfoTableEntries(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Frees all IO info table entries during CRT cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through g_apIoInfoTable array (64 entries, 0x6fc52220-0x6fc52320)\n2. For each non-null entry, iterate through embedded structures at stride 0x24 (36 bytes)\n3. Delete CRITICAL_SECTION at offset 0xC if SpinCount (offset 0x8) is non-zero\n4. Free the block memory via FUN_6fc4719c and clear the table entry\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480 (1152): Total bytes per table entry (32 structures * 36 bytes)\n- 0x24 (36): Stride between IO info structures\n- 0xC (12): Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION within each structure\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CRTDllMainHandler: Caller (DLL cleanup context)\n- FUN_6fc4719c: Block memory free function",
