      "name": "InitCmdLineArgs",
      "signature": "void InitCmdLineArgs(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes command-line argument parsing for C runtime startup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Ensure environment is initialized (call FUN_6fc49960 if not)\n2. Get module file path via GetModuleFileNameA\n3. Select command source: g_szCmdLine if non-empty, else module path\n4. Call ParseCmdLineArgs to count arguments and total characters needed\n5. Allocate buffer for argv array plus concatenated strings\n6. Call ParseCmdLineArgs again to populate argv array\n7. Store argc-1 in g_nArgC, argv pointer in g_pszArgV\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global g_szCmdLine)\n\nReturns:\n- void (global argv/argc set on success, calls __amsg_exit(8) on alloc failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size\n- 8: __amsg_exit code for insufficient memory",
