      "name": "ParseCmdLineArgs",
      "signature": "void ParseCmdLineArgs(byte * pbCmdLine, char * * ppszArgV, byte * pbArgBuf, int * pnArgCount, int * pnCharCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses command line string into argc/argv style arguments.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output counts: nCharCount=0, nArgCount=1\n2. Store first argv entry pointer if ppszArgV is provided\n3. Parse first argument (program name):\n   - If starts with quote (0x22): extract until closing quote\n   - Else: extract until whitespace or null\n4. Skip whitespace delimiters between arguments\n5. For each remaining argument:\n   a. Count consecutive backslashes\n   b. Handle quote: even backslashes = toggle quote mode, emit N/2 backslashes\n   c. Handle lead bytes (multi-byte chars) via g_abCharTypeTable lookup\n   d. Copy character to output buffer if provided\n6. Null-terminate each argument string\n7. Store NULL sentinel in argv array, increment final counts\n\nParameters:\n- pbCmdLine: Input command line string to parse\n- ppszArgV: Output argv array (NULL for count-only pass)\n- pbArgBuf: Buffer for null-terminated arg strings (NULL for count-only)\n- pnArgCount: Output argc (includes final NULL entry)\n- pnCharCount: Output total characters including terminators\n\nReturns:\n- void (results via pnArgCount and pnCharCount pointers)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x22 (34): Double quote ASCII\n- 0x5c (92): Backslash ASCII\n- 0x20 (32): Space ASCII\n- 0x09 (9): Tab ASCII\n- 0x04: Lead byte flag in character type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
