      "name": "GetStringTypeInternal",
      "signature": "BOOL GetStringTypeInternal(DWORD dwInfoType, LPCSTR lpszSrcStr, int nLen, LPWORD lpCharType, UINT uCodePage, LCID lcid, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Gets character type information for a string, auto-selecting Unicode or ANSI API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If g_nStringTypeMode uninitialized (0), probe system capabilities:\n   - Try GetStringTypeW first; if succeeds, set mode=1 (Unicode)\n   - Else try GetStringTypeA; if succeeds, set mode=2 (ANSI)\n   - If both fail, return 0\n2. If mode=2 (ANSI path): call GetStringTypeA directly with locale\n3. If mode=1 (Unicode path):\n   - Convert multibyte source to wide chars via MultiByteToWideChar\n   - Call GetStringTypeW on converted buffer\n   - nFlags controls MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS (bit 3)\n\nParameters:\n- dwInfoType: CT_CTYPE1/2/3 info type constant\n- lpszSrcStr: Source multibyte string\n- nLen: Source string length (-1 for null-terminated)\n- lpCharType: Output buffer for character type info\n- uCodePage: Code page (0 = use g_uDefaultCodePage)\n- lcid: Locale ID (0 = use g_dwLocaleCodePage)\n- nFlags: If non-zero, adds MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS flag\n\nReturns:\n- TRUE on success, FALSE on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 1: Unicode mode / CT_CTYPE1 / dwFlags base\n- 2: ANSI mode\n- 8: MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a7046d73bbd286a50d5e7204509858d2",
