      "name": "WriteValidateHandle",
      "signature": "int WriteValidateHandle(uint dwFileHandle, char * szBuffer, uint dwCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates file handle and performs write with locking (CRT _write wrapper).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dwFileHandle < g_dwIoHandleCount\n2. Look up IO info entry via g_apIoInfoTable[handle >> 5] + (handle & 0x1F) * 0x24\n3. Verify bit 0 set in flags byte at offset +4 (handle is open/valid)\n4. If valid: lock handle, call FUN_6fc474ff to write, unlock, return bytes written\n5. If invalid: set errno=EBADF (9), doserrno=0, return -1\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileHandle (uint): CRT file descriptor to write to\n- szBuffer (char*): Source buffer to write from\n- dwCount (uint): Number of bytes to write\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes written on success (from FUN_6fc474ff)\n- -1 on invalid handle (sets errno=9 EBADF)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): IO info structure stride\n- 0x1F: Mask for index within IO table bucket (32 entries per bucket)\n- 0x5: Bit shift for bucket index (32 entries = 2^5)\n- 9: errno value EBADF (bad file descriptor)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:bac569fc88fbfeebd4a5205bbcce1faf",
