      "name": "LockFilePointer",
      "signature": "void LockFilePointer(FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquires lock for FILE pointer based on its storage location.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pFile is within CRT internal iob[] array (0x6fc4e458 - 0x6fc4e6b8)\n2. If internal: Calculate lock index from array offset, acquire via LockCrtCriticalSection\n3. If external: Enter the embedded CRITICAL_SECTION at pFile+0x20\n\nParameters:\n- pFile (FILE*): File pointer to lock\n\nReturns:\n- void (holds lock on return)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6fc4e458: Start of internal _iob[] array\n- 0x6fc4e6b8: End of internal _iob[] array\n- 0x20 (32): Offset to embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in FILE structure\n- 0x1c (28): Base lock index for file streams in g_apCritSectTable",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ff70d7fac2548b5958f726d1eeb33c1c",
