      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Thread-safe wrapper for wide character to multibyte conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment locale lock count atomically\n2. If lock limit is set, release lock count and acquire critical section 0x13\n3. Call internal conversion function (WideCharToMultiByte)\n4. Release critical section or decrement lock count based on path taken\n5. Return converted string result\n\nParameters:\n- lpszDest (LPSTR): Destination buffer for multibyte character\n- wcChar (WCHAR): Wide character to convert\n\nReturns:\n- LPSTR: Number of bytes written on success, -1 on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x13: CRT critical section ID for locale operations",
