      "name": "CompareStrings",
      "signature": "int CompareStrings(char * lpszStr1, char * lpszStr2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Compares two null-terminated strings lexicographically with DWORD alignment optimization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if lpszStr1 is DWORD-aligned (address & 0x3)\n2. If not aligned, compare bytes until alignment achieved\n3. Main loop: Load 4 bytes at a time from aligned lpszStr1\n4. Compare each byte with corresponding byte in lpszStr2\n5. Check for null terminator after each byte comparison\n6. Return result when mismatch or null terminator found\n\nParameters:\n- lpszStr1 (char*): First null-terminated string to compare\n- lpszStr2 (char*): Second null-terminated string to compare\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Strings are equal\n- -1: lpszStr1 is lexicographically less than lpszStr2\n- 1: lpszStr1 is lexicographically greater than lpszStr2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Mask for DWORD alignment check (3 = 0b11)\n- 0x1: Mask for byte alignment check\n- 0x2: Mask for word alignment check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f93a26193b15127770b523718dea2fb3",
