      "name": "InitializeSbhHeapBlock",
      "signature": "int InitializeSbhHeapBlock(int nThreshold)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes the Small Block Heap (SBH) block array for CRT memory management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0x140 bytes from g_hCrtHeap for block array\n2. Returns 0 immediately if allocation fails\n3. Clears g_nSbhBlockIndex and g_nHeapBlockCount to 0\n4. Sets g_pSbhBlockCurrent to allocated array base\n5. Stores threshold parameter in g_dwSbhThreshold\n6. Sets initial capacity to 0x10 blocks\n\nParameters:\n- nThreshold (int): Maximum allocation size for small block heap routing\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (block array allocated and initialized)\n- 0 on failure (HeapAlloc returned NULL)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x140 (320): Initial heap block array allocation size\n- 0x10 (16): Initial block capacity count",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a57b3ae583e4f6f104245d4da8d3b9fe",
