      "name": "FindHeapBlockByAddress",
      "signature": "uint FindHeapBlockByAddress(void * pAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Finds the heap block entry containing the specified address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through g_pHeapBlockArray (stride 0x14)\n2. For each block, check if pAddress is within 0x100000 bytes of block base (offset 0xC)\n3. Return pointer to matching heap block entry, or 0 if not found\n\nParameters:\n- pAddress (void*): Memory address to look up in heap block table\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to heap block entry (20-byte struct) if found, 0 otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Heap block entry size/stride\n- 0xC (12): Offset to heap base address within entry\n- 0x100000 (1MB): Maximum heap block size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
