      "name": "SbhCreateBlock",
      "signature": "void * SbhCreateBlock(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a new Small Block Heap (SBH) block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If block array is at capacity, expand via HeapReAlloc (add 16 entries)\n2. Calculate block entry pointer at g_pHeapBlockArray[g_nHeapBlockCount]\n3. Allocate 0x41c4-byte control structure via HeapAlloc\n4. Reserve 1MB virtual address space via VirtualAlloc (MEM_RESERVE)\n5. Initialize block entry fields and increment block count\n6. Set first DWORD of control structure to -1 (empty indicator)\n\nParameters:\n- None (reads global state: g_nHeapBlockCount, g_nSbhBlockCapacity, g_pHeapBlockArray)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to initialized block entry on success\n- NULL on allocation failure (HeapReAlloc, HeapAlloc, or VirtualAlloc)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Block entry structure stride (5 DWORDs)\n- 0x41c4 (16836): Control structure size\n- 0x100000 (1MB): Virtual memory reservation size\n- 0x2000: MEM_RESERVE flag\n- 0xffffffff: Empty/invalid marker",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
