      "name": "SbhResizeBlockInPlace",
      "signature": "int SbhResizeBlockInPlace(uint * pHeapInfo, byte * pBlock, int nNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Attempts to resize a small-block heap (SBH) allocation in-place.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align requested size to 16-byte boundary (nNewSize + 0x17 & ~0xF)\n2. Calculate group index from block offset (offset >> 15)\n3. Get current block size from header at pBlock-4\n4. If current < aligned new size, try to coalesce with next free block:\n   - Check next block is free (low bit = 0) and combined size sufficient\n   - Unlink next block from free list and update bitmaps\n   - Create remainder free block if space left over\n5. If current > aligned new size, split block:\n   - Shrink current allocation and create free block from remainder\n   - Optionally coalesce remainder with following free block\n6. Update block headers with new size (+1 for in-use flag)\n\nParameters:\n- pHeapInfo (uint*): Heap info structure with bitmaps at offsets 0,4\n- pBlock (byte*): Pointer to allocated block data\n- nNewSize (int): Requested new size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (block resized in-place)\n- 0 on failure (need to reallocate elsewhere)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10: Alignment (16 bytes)\n- 0x17: Alignment rounding constant\n- 0x0F: Size class computation mask\n- 0x3F (63): Maximum bucket index (64 size classes)\n- 0x20 (32): Split between low/high bitmap words\n- 0x204: Group stride in bytes\n- 0x144: Base offset for free lists\n- 0x44/0xC4: Group bitmap array offsets\n- 0x80000000: Bit mask MSB for bitmap operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e4f799c77acab14c5b1bdda2181c2d46",
