      "name": "CreateSmallBlockHeapRegion",
      "signature": "void * * CreateSmallBlockHeapRegion(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Creates a new small-block heap region for CRT memory allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate region descriptor (0x2020 bytes) from heap or use static one\n2. Reserve 4MB virtual memory (MEM_RESERVE 0x2000)\n3. Commit first 64KB (MEM_COMMIT 0x1000)\n4. Insert region into doubly-linked list (g_pSbhRegionHead/Tail)\n5. Initialize 1024 free block size entries (8 bytes each)\n6. Zero the committed memory and set up page headers\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to region descriptor on success\n- NULL on allocation failure (cleans up partial allocations)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2020: Region descriptor size (header + 1024 size entries * 8)\n- 0x400000: 4MB reserved virtual memory per region\n- 0x10000: 64KB initial committed memory\n- 0x400: 1024 free block size classes\n- 0xF1: Sentinel value for size class entries\n- 0x1000: Page size stride (4KB)\n- 0xF0: Initial page free block count",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b10e654b1e0872dc227e39198444a376",
