      "name": "DecommitEmptySbhPages",
      "signature": "void DecommitEmptySbhPages(int nMaxPages)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Decommits empty pages from small block heap regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through SBH regions starting from tail\n2. For each region with valid base address (not -1)\n3. Scan page entries backwards (0x3FF000 to 0, stride 0x1000)\n4. Pages marked 0xF0 are candidates - call VirtualFree(MEM_DECOMMIT)\n5. On success, mark page as -1 and update first-free pointer\n6. If all 1024 pages in region are decommitted, free entire region\n7. Stop after nMaxPages pages decommitted or all regions scanned\n\nParameters:\n- nMaxPages (int): Maximum number of pages to decommit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xF0: Page fully free, candidate for decommit\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1): Page already decommitted\n- 0x1000: Page size (4KB)\n- 0x4000: MEM_DECOMMIT flag\n- 0x400 (1024): Pages per region\n- 0x804: Offset to last page entry in region header",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4356a93c484fa354f7841c9d1d714a19",
