      "name": "GetTlsOsErrorField",
      "signature": "DWORD * GetTlsOsErrorField(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Returns pointer to OS error code field in thread-local storage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetOrAllocTlsData to get TLS data pointer\n2. Add 0xc (12 bytes) to get pointer to error field at index 3\n3. Return the computed pointer\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- DWORD* pointer to TLS error field at offset 0xc\n- Never returns NULL (GetOrAllocTlsData guarantees valid pointer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc (12): Byte offset to OS error field in TLS structure",
