      "name": "GetOsHandleFromCrtHandle",
      "signature": "dword GetOsHandleFromCrtHandle(dword dwCrtHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a CRT file handle to its corresponding OS (Windows) handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate handle index is within g_dwIoHandleCount\n2. Compute table index: chunk = handle >> 5, slot = handle & 0x1f\n3. Check validity flag (byte at IoInfo+4, bit 0) is set\n4. Return OS handle from IoInfo offset 0, or -1 on error\n\nParameters:\n- dwCrtHandle (dword): CRT runtime file handle index\n\nReturns:\n- OS handle (HANDLE) on success\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on invalid handle, sets errno=9 (EBADF)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): IoInfo structure stride\n- 0x1f (31): Slot mask for 32-entry chunks\n- 0x5: Bit shift for chunk index (divide by 32)\n- 9: EBADF (bad file descriptor) errno value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:925a8d581e90d1850e90a2aaf94686cb",
