      "name": "FlushFileStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "int FlushFileStreamBuffer(FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes a file stream buffer to disk.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fc4a01e to write pending buffer data to file handle\n2. If write fails, return -1 (error)\n3. If commit flag (0x40 at offset 0xd) is set, flush OS file buffers\n4. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n- pFile (FILE*): Pointer to FILE stream structure\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure (write error or OS flush failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xd: Offset to file flags byte in FILE structure\n- 0x40: Commit/sync flag - forces OS buffer flush when set\n- 0x10: Offset to file descriptor (param_1[4]) in FILE structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
