      "name": "FlushWriteBuffer",
      "signature": "int FlushWriteBuffer(int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes pending write buffer data to the underlying file handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stream is in write mode (flags & 3 == 2) and has dirty data (flags & 0x108)\n2. Calculate bytes to write: current position - buffer base\n3. If bytes > 0, call WriteValidateHandle to write buffer contents\n4. On success with text mode (0x80), clear write flag (0x02)\n5. On failure, set error flag (0x20) and return -1\n6. Reset buffer count to 0 and position to base\n\nParameters:\n- pStream (int*): FILE stream structure pointer\n  - [0]: Current buffer position\n  - [1]: Buffer count\n  - [2]: Buffer base pointer  \n  - [3]: Flags (mode, error, dirty)\n  - [4]: OS file handle\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success or no data to flush\n- -1 on write error\n\nFlag Bits:\n- 0x02: Write mode active\n- 0x20: Error occurred\n- 0x80: Text/CRLF translation mode\n- 0x108: Buffer has dirty data",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4c053343a65baac58fac65c0d3534b2b",
