      "name": "SbhMemmove",
      "signature": "void * SbhMemmove(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint nSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copies nSize bytes from pSrc to pDest, handling overlapping regions correctly.\n\nThis is the CRT memmove implementation used by the Small Block Heap (SBH).\nIt safely handles the case where source and destination memory regions overlap.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dest > src AND dest < src + size (overlapping backward)\n2. If overlapping: set pointers to end, copy backward using STD+REP MOVSD\n3. If not overlapping: copy forward using REP MOVSD for efficiency\n4. Handle unaligned start by copying 1-3 leading bytes to reach alignment\n5. Bulk copy aligned DWORDs (8+ at a time uses REP MOVSD)\n6. Copy trailing 0-3 bytes via computed jump table\n\nParameters:\n- pDest (void*): Destination buffer address\n- pSrc (void*): Source buffer address  \n- nSize (uint): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- pDest pointer unchanged (allows call chaining)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Bitmask for 4-byte alignment check\n- 0x8 (8): Minimum DWORDs for REP MOVSD optimization\n- 0x4: DWORD size in bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
