      "name": "CharToUpperWithLocale",
      "signature": "uint CharToUpperWithLocale(void * this, uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Converts a character to uppercase using locale settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If no locale codepage set, use ASCII conversion (a-z to A-Z via -0x20)\n2. For locale mode, check if char < 0x100 and has lowercase flag (bit 2)\n3. Check high byte in char type table for DBCS lead byte (bit 0x80)\n4. Call LCMapStringWithLocale with LCMAP_UPPERCASE (0x200) flag\n5. Return single or double byte result based on output length\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Locale context pointer (unused directly)\n- dwChar (uint): Character to convert (single or double byte)\n\nReturns:\n- Uppercase character value (single byte or DBCS)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
