      "name": "CommitOsFileHandle",
      "signature": "int CommitOsFileHandle(uint dwCrtHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Commits pending I/O data to disk for a CRT file handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwCrtHandle is within g_dwIoHandleCount bounds\n2. Calculate IoInfo table index: entry = handle >> 5, slot = handle & 0x1F\n3. Check handle validity flag (bit 0 of flags at offset 0x4)\n4. Lock the I/O handle via LockIoHandle for thread safety\n5. Re-check validity flag (may have changed after lock)\n6. Get underlying OS HANDLE via GetOsHandleFromCrtHandle\n7. Call FlushFileBuffers to commit buffered data to disk\n8. On failure, retrieve OS error and store in TLS fields\n9. Unlock handle via UnlockIoHandle\n10. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n- dwCrtHandle (uint): CRT file descriptor index into IoInfo table\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success (data committed to disk)\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) on failure with errno set to EBADF (9)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1F (31): Mask for slot within IoInfo table entry\n- 0x24 (36): IoInfo structure stride in bytes\n- 0x5: Right shift for table entry index (32 handles per entry)\n- 0x1: Handle validity flag bitmask\n- 0x9: EBADF errno value (bad file descriptor)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b14dfb771e9c85951130aa7c0ee6e7bc",
